              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "I intermittently see the top carousel bit either not load anything or not load the text. But usually after reload it's fine. So I suspect there's some timing issue.",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "I intermittently see the top carousel bit either not load anything or not load the text. But usually after reload it's fine. So I suspect there's some timing issue.",
              "time": "2026-04-13T15:23:26Z"
            },
            {
              "attachment_id": null,
              "author": "jmuizelaar@mozilla.com",
              "bug_id": 2030614,
              "count": 4,
              "creation_time": "2026-04-15T13:58:06Z",
              "creator": "jmuizelaar@mozilla.com",
              "id": 18017444,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "We tried diagnosing this today and were seeing a bunch of broken stuff. It mostly seems like the server is not working well and is very slow to respond to requests. This may be causing timing brokenness.\n\nThe carousel text gets set by https://s.yimg.com/aaq/wf/wf-text-1.2.0.js in this kind of function:\n```js\n key: \"stateDidUpdate\",\n                    value: function() {\n                        var e = this._util.text;\n                        if (void 0 !== e) {\n                            var t = this._util.elem;\n                            c.destroy(t, {\n                                destroySelf: !1\n                            }),\n                            t.innerHTML = e,\n                            c.sync(t)\n                        }\n                    }\n```",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "We tried diagnosing this today and were seeing a bunch of broken stuff. It mostly seems like the server is not working well and is very slow to respond to requests. This may be causing timing brokenness.\n\nThe carousel text gets set by https://s.yimg.com/aaq/wf/wf-text-1.2.0.js in this kind of function:\n```js\n key: \"stateDidUpdate\",\n                    value: function() {\n                        var e = this._util.text;\n                        if (void 0 !== e) {\n                            var t = this._util.elem;\n                            c.destroy(t, {\n                                destroySelf: !1\n                            }),\n                            t.innerHTML = e,\n                            c.sync(t)\n                        }\n                    }\n```",
              "time": "2026-04-15T13:58:06Z"
            },
